# No Push Until Asked

- **Never run `git push`** (or push to remote in any form) unless the user explicitly asks in that conversation (e.g. "push", "push to main").
- Committing is still governed by the user's commit rule — only commit when explicitly asked.
- After making changes, stop at commit-ready state or report what changed locally; do not push proactively, even for bug fixes or urgent regressions.
- If the user says "save" or "don't push until I say", treat that as an ongoing preference until they explicitly request a push.
